Error: Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge: `big` is too large for `#Inline(Always)`
  --> Tests/UI/inline_always_too_large.jet:3:1
    |
  3 | #Inline(Always) big: fn() -> Int {
    | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Its body has 44 statements, over the 40-statement ceiling that keeps the copy at every call site small. `#Inline(Always)` guarantees that every direct call is inlined on every tier, or the program is refused: sema refuses a function that calls itself or closes a cycle of marked calls (Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways), one used as a value (Jet.InlineAlwaysAddressTaken), one over the size ceiling (Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge), a `#Scrub` routine (Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub), one that reads `context.trace` (Jet.InlineAlwaysReadsTrace) and one with a foreign body (Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign).
 Fix: Drop `#Inline(Always)` (use `#Inline` as a hint the compiler is free to ignore), or split the function so the hot part is small enough to inline.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge
